# The two SDK bundles under the path that names their version never change once
# released, so a browser keeps them for a year without asking again. Every other
# path, the unversioned SDK paths included, keeps the asset default: revalidated
# on each use. The rules name the two files exactly, so no other answer under
# /sdk/ can carry the header. The deploy's package step accepts only these
# rules (scripts/stamp-workflow.mjs); a new SDK version changes the two paths.
/sdk/0.2.0/edge-personalization.esm.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/sdk/0.2.0/edge-personalization.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
